# Web terminal broker selection
# A setting without # is ENABLED. A setting starting with # is DISABLED.
# Enable ONE complete broker block; do not mix settings from different brokers.
# Change only the VITE_ setting lines. Keep headings and explanations commented.
#
# EXAMPLE: SWITCH FROM TEST TO ACHIEVER
# 1. Add # before every VITE_ setting in the TEST block.
# 2. Remove # before every VITE_ setting in the Achiever Financials block.
# 3. Keep the MyProp, Grow Trading Academy, and legacy blocks commented.
# 4. Stop the running server with Ctrl+C, then run: npm run dev:web
# 5. Refresh the browser and log in with your Achiever account.
# Changing brokers requires a fresh login; saved accounts and preferences remain.
# For production, run npm run build:web and deploy the new dist folder.
#
# runtime-config.js is generated automatically; do not edit it manually.
# Duplicate active broker settings stop startup instead of mixing brokers.
# If another broker still appears, check .env.web.local and VITE_ variables set
# in your terminal: they can override this file through Vite's normal precedence.
#
# WHAT THE SETTINGS MEAN
# BACKEND_URL / API_URL / RTX5_API_URL / FIX_API_URL / API_HOST / API_HOST_EXT:
#   HTTP API addresses used by different app modules for login and trading data.
#   Keep all supplied API addresses together with their broker block.
# WS_URL / FIX_WS_URL / MARKET_WS_URL: websocket addresses for live updates.
# WS_HOST: the websocket base address, without the /ws/v2 path.
# BROKER_DISCOVERY_URL / DISCOVERY_BASE_URL: directory used to find broker servers.
# BROKER_ID: selects the broker shown by this web terminal.
# FEED_BROKER_ID: identifies that broker to the market-data feed; it can differ
#   from BROKER_ID, as shown in the Grow Trading Academy block.
# DEFAULT_MT5_SERVER: the broker's default login server name.
# FEED_BROKER_TOKEN: this broker's feed credential, if required. Keep the supplied
#   value with its broker; an empty value means no token is configured here.
#   VITE_ values are visible to the browser; never put an account password here.

# Shared web settings (keep enabled)
# Use the web/browser backend configuration for this run.
# VITE_BACKEND_TARGET=web
# VITE_BACKEND_MODE=web
# # false uses the real broker directory instead of mock discovery data.
# VITE_USE_MOCK_DISCOVERY=false
# # true enables diagnostic logging; use false for a production build.
# VITE_ENABLE_DEBUG=true

